            (see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/302038/381"} this MO discussion
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS3%2FCFT2"} AdS3/CFT2
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original BTZ black hole with trivial internal topology is due to:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M%C3%A1ximo+Ba%C3%B1ados"}> Máximo Bañados
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Teitelboim"} Claudio Teitelboim
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Zanelli"} Jorge Zanelli
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Black Hole in Three Dimensional Space Time
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9204099"} arXiv:hep-th/9204099
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M%C3%A1ximo+Ba%C3%B1ados"}> Máximo Bañados
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"} Marc Henneaux
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Teitelboim"} Claudio Teitelboim
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Zanelli"} Jorge Zanelli
              %p
                %em> Geometry of the 2+1 Black Hole
                , Phys. Rev. D48: 1506-1525, 1993 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9302012"}> arXiv:gr-qc/9302012
                )
          %p The generalization to arbitrary black holes in 2+1-dimensional AdS gravity, with generally non-trivial internal topology:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Stefan Aminneborg,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingemar+Bengtsson"} Ingemar Bengtsson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Black Holes and Wormholes in 2+1 Dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9707036"} arXiv:gr-qc/9707036
            %li
              %p
                Stefan Aminneborg,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingemar+Bengtsson"} Ingemar Bengtsson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Spinning Anti-de Sitter Wormhole
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9805028"} arXiv:gr-qc/9805028
            %li
              %p
                Dieter Brill,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Black Holes and Wormholes in 2+1 Dimensions
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Mathematical and Quantum Aspects of Relativity and Cosmology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9904083"} arXiv:gr-qc/9904083
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-46671-1_6"} doi:10.1007/3-540-46671-1_6
                )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Aritra Ghosh, Chandrasekhar Bhamidipati,
                %em Thermodynamic geometry and interacting microstructures of BTZ black holes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.10510"}> arXiv:2001.10510
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roberto+Emparan"}> Roberto Emparan
                , Antonia Micol Frassino, Benson Way,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum BTZ black hole
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.15999"} arXiv:2007.15999
            %li
              %p
                Pablo Bueno, Pablo A. Cano, Javier Moreno, Guido van der Velde,
                %em Regular black holes in three dimensions
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.10172"}> arXiv:2104.10172
                )
            %li
              %p
                Matías Briceño, Cristián Martínez,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Zanelli"} Jorge Zanelli
                %em On the central singularity of the BTZ geometries
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.06552"}> arXiv:2404.06552
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            In view of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+censorship+hypothesis"} cosmic censorship hypothesis
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roberto+Emparan"}> Roberto Emparan
              , Marija Tomašević,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Strong cosmic censorship in the BTZ black hole
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.02083"} arXiv:2002.02083
          %p
            Via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+M-theory"} topological M-theory
          %ul
            %li
              Javier Chagoya, Graciela Reyes-Ahumada, M. Sabido,
              %em BTZ entropy from topological M-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.01094"}> arXiv:2011.01094
              )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BTZ_black_hole"} BTZ black hole
          %h3#euclidean_btz_black_holes Euclidean BTZ black holes
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+field+theory"} Euclidean
